# Race start — Grand Prix / Novice / Jack Cup / Mute City / Blue Falcon.
#
# Everything after the title is gated on gGameMode with WAITMODE rather than on a frame count,
# because the boot timeline is wall-clock-coupled (see title.script and refbuild-progress.md) and
# a fixed wait that is long enough on a warm run overshoots a menu on a cold one. The three gates
# are GAMEMODE_MAIN_MENU (7), GAMEMODE_MACHINE_SELECT (8), GAMEMODE_MACHINE_SETTINGS (9) and
# GAMEMODE_GP_RACE (1) from decomp/include/fzx_game.h. A WAITMODE that times out logs
# "[autotest] WAITMODE timeout" and CONTINUES, so read the log before trusting any shot below it —
# CONTINUING.md says exactly this about scripts that claim to have raced.
#
# Menu path (every step is the A button on an "OK?" prompt; START only leaves the title):
#   TITLE -START-> SELECT MODE -A-> class popup -A-> NOVICE -A-> cup -A-> Jack Cup
#         -A-> MUTE CITY -A-> SELECT MACHINE -A-> BLUE FALCON -A-> settings -A-> OK -A-> RACE
# 400, not 1500: the staged config paces the loop at 59.94 Hz, which puts the title window at
# roughly poll 300-900 (unpaced it is near 1200-1500). At 1500 this script was pressing START
# inside the attract-mode demo race.
WAIT 400
SHOT race_title
PRESS START 10
WAITMODE 7 600
LOG reached SELECT MODE
WAIT 60
PRESS A 10
WAIT 90
PRESS A 10
WAIT 90
PRESS A 10
WAIT 120
SHOT race_cup
PRESS A 10
WAIT 120
SHOT race_course
PRESS A 10
WAITMODE 8 600
LOG reached SELECT MACHINE
WAIT 60
SHOT race_machine
PRESS A 10
WAIT 120
PRESS A 10
WAITMODE 9 600
LOG reached MACHINE SETTINGS
WAIT 60
SHOT race_settings
PRESS A 10
WAIT 90
PRESS A 10
WAITMODE 1 1200
LOG reached GP RACE
WAIT 150
SHOT race_grid
WAIT 240
SHOT race_start
WAIT 10
QUIT
